1. Privacy Policy — Hunt’s Privacy Guard
Last updated: October 18, 2026
Hunt’s Privacy Guard helps users block submissions containing terms on their protected list. This policy explains what the extension checks, what it stores, and whether it shares information.
Information the extension handles
When protection is turned on, the extension checks text in supported website text fields when the user attempts to submit it. It compares that text with the protected terms saved in the extension. If a term matches, the extension blocks the submission.
The extension stores the protected terms, protection setting, PIN-related data, and new-tab page preference in Chrome’s extension storage on the user’s device. It keeps a blocked-submission count for the current browser session. If the user uses the PIN recovery feature, the extension can save a recovery text file through Chrome Downloads.
Sharing and collection
Hunt’s Privacy Guard does not send the checked text, protected terms, PIN-related data, or blocked-submission count to the developer or to a server. The extension does not sell or share this information with third parties.
User control and limitations
Users can edit their protected list, turn protection on or off, and remove the extension through Chrome’s extension settings. The extension only checks supported text fields on pages where Chrome allows extensions to run. It cannot guarantee that every kind of personal information will be detected or blocked.
