2. Chrome Web Store privacy disclosures and permission justifications
Single purpose
Hunt’s Privacy Guard helps users protect personal information by checking text submitted through supported website fields against a user-managed list of protected terms and blocking matching submissions.
Permission justifications
Host permissions: All websites (<all_urls>)
The extension needs access to pages across websites so it can detect supported text fields and check their contents when a user attempts to submit a message or form. This check happens locally in the browser. The extension does not transmit the page text to the developer or a server. Chrome-internal pages and other restricted pages may not allow the extension to run.
Storage
The extension uses Chrome storage to keep the user’s protected terms and settings on the device. Session storage is used for the current session’s blocked-submission count.
Downloads
The extension uses Chrome Downloads to save a PIN recovery text file when the user requests recovery.
User data disclosure
The extension handles text entered into supported website fields to compare it with the user’s protected list before submission. Matching text is blocked. The extension stores the protected list and settings locally in Chrome extension storage. It does not transmit, sell, or share checked text or stored extension data with the developer or third parties.
